  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n-  Showers and thunderstorms today through Saturday.\n\n-  Warming and drying Sunday through early next week.\n\n\nA low pressure system will have an impacted on the Northern\nRockies for the next couple of days as surges of moisture and\nenergy make their way through the region. Latest radar data is\nindicating the first round of storms is currently over southern\nIdaho and will be making their way into Lemhi county and southwest\nMontana later this morning. This first round of storms will\ndiminish the farther north it goes this morning. The next round of\nthunderstorms will develop south of the I-90 corridor this\nafternoon into the evening. These storms will be stronger and\ncapable of producing moderate to heavy rain, lightning and gusty\nwinds. These storms will push north I-90 after sunset and diminish\nin intensity.\n\nFriday afternoon another round of showers and thunderstorms will\ndevelop across the Northern Rockies. The extent of these storms\nappear to stretch south of the line from Glacier National park to\nLookout pass. Once again these storms will be capable of moderate\nto heavy rainfall, gusty winds and this time small hail. \n\nThen on Saturday the low pressure system begins to exit the region\ncausing wrap around precipitation. The main focus of the\nprecipitation appears to stay south of the highway 12 corridor.\nThe bulk of the precipitation type will be light stratiform rain,\nso at this time not expected any strong storms. \n\nA ridge of high pressure is expected to build over the region\nSunday into the first part of next week causing a warming and\ndrying trend.",
